.TH ZSTD-SPLITTER 1 "2026-07-26" "zstd-splitter 4.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zstd-splitter \- tar compression, splitting, strict integrity and SSH network Swiss-Knife
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zstd-splitter
.BR -c " ... [" -R " destination] source"
.br
.B zstd-splitter
.BR -P " -i -R destination [" -O " name=value] input"
.br
.B zstd-splitter
.BR -G " -i -R remote-input [" -d " directory]"
.br
.B zstd-splitter
.BR -Q " mode -R destination"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Version 4.1 is a cumulative release of the 4.x Network Swiss-Knife. Local archive operations remain compatible with version 3. Network transfers use SSH and SFTP, strict SHA-256 manifests, remote staging, per-archive locks and atomic bundle publication.
.SH NETWORK OPTIONS
.TP
.BI -R " spec"
Remote specification in the form [user@]host:/absolute/path.
.TP
.BI -O " name=value"
Set a network option. May be repeated.
.TP
.BI -F " file"
Read network options from a configuration file.
.TP
.B -P
Push a local strict archive or part set.
.TP
.B -G
Pull and verify a remote archive or part set.
.TP
.BI -Q " mode"
Run network, health, inventory, gc or config query. Availability depends on the release version.
.TP
.B -Y
Relay a strict part set between SSH hosts without local payload storage. Version 4.2 only.
.SH PROFILES
Version 4.1 and later provide safe, lan, jumbo-lan, wan, high-latency, metered, unstable and archive profiles. Jumbo-frame diagnostics never modify MTU or kernel settings.
.SH FILES
.I /usr/local/bin/zstd-splitter
.br
.I /usr/local/share/man/man1/zstd-splitter.1.gz
.SH SECURITY
Host-key checking defaults to strict. Network publication should use strict integrity. SHA-256 is an integrity mechanism, not a signature.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ssh (1),
.BR sftp (1),
.BR tar (1),
.BR sha256sum (1)
